  shared libraries as separate, replaceable files on disk, so the LGPL-3.0
  option stays genuinely exercisable by any downstream re-user who prefers it,
  and it keeps the bundled licenses/ folder visible to the end user instead of
  sealed inside a self-extracting blob.

